*.nims
# ct_test ships a checked-in NimScript config that resolves the runquota_process
# import paths from RUNQUOTA_SRC when the relative sibling layout is unavailable
# (git worktrees, CI). It must be tracked despite the blanket *.nims ignore.
!src/ct_test/config.nims
# NS1's host-free build gate ships its own NimScript config: it is half of the
# poison (the `patchFile` bans and the stubs search path), and without it
# `ci/test/hostfree-build.sh` cannot even find `stubs/no_host_access`. Tracked
# despite the blanket *.nims ignore, for the same reason as the line above.
!ci/hostfree/config.nims
# ct_test C/C++ provider fixtures build into an in-tree build/ directory and the
# provider suites compile to bare (extension-less) binaries next to their .nim
# sources; both are reproducible test artifacts that must not be committed.
src/ct_test/fixtures/*/build/
src/ct_test/*_test
# The incremental-runner suites compile to bare (extension-less) binaries next
# to their .nim sources via `nim c -r`; those are reproducible test artifacts.
src/ct_test/incremental/test_*
!src/ct_test/incremental/test_*.nim
src/ct_test/incremental/e2e_*
!src/ct_test/incremental/e2e_*.nim
*.log
format.js
config/.config.yaml
/.config.yaml
src/tests/trace_index.db
# SQLite's WAL journal and shared-memory index. They are created beside the
# database whenever a lane run opens it in WAL mode and are removed only on a
# clean close, so a lane that is interrupted (or that leaves a connection to
# the OS to reap) leaves them behind. Ignoring the database but not these two
# left every ViewModel lane run showing two untracked files.
src/tests/trace_index.db-shm
src/tests/trace_index.db-wal
# The lang-name migration writes a backup beside the database before it
# rewrites it, so a test run leaves one of these behind. The database itself is
# ignored; its backup is the same thing one step older.
src/tests/trace_index.db.*.bak
